==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|evidently}}, {{m|enm|evydently}}; equivalent to {{af|en|evident|-ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɛvɪdəntli/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-evidently.ogg|a=US}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a manner which makes the fact or conclusion [[evident]]; [[obviously]]; as may be clearly inferred. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|The Elopers|33|The half-dozen pieces {{...}} were painted white and carved with festoons of flowers, birds and cupids. To display them the walls had been tinted a vivid blue which had now faded, but the carpet, which had '''evidently''' been stored and recently relaid, retained its original turquoise.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} In such a way as to be clearly [[visible]] or [[manifest]]; [[distinctly]], [[clearly]]. {{defdate|14th|19th c.}}
#* {{RQ:Tyndale NT|Acts|10|3|clxviij|versoend=1|The ſame mã ſawe in a vyſion '''evydently''' aboute the nynthe houre of the daye the angell of god commynge in vnto hym {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|proscribed}} [[apparently]]

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|obviously|as may be clearly inferred}} {{l|en|clearly}}, {{l|en|plainly}}; see also [[Thesaurus:obviously]]
* {{sense|clearly visible}} {{l|en|conspicuously}}, {{l|en|markedly}}, {{l|en|vividly}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|self-evidently}}

